1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,891
This is Lunar Site Planner.

2
00:00:02,891 --> 00:00:04,275
In under two minutes,

3
00:00:04,275 --> 00:00:07,760
I'll show you how to plan a Moon landing in Professional mode,

4
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:10,117
from picking a site to sharing a report.

5
00:00:10,767 --> 00:00:12,881
On the left is your mission flow:

6
00:00:12,881 --> 00:00:14,344
five steps, in order.

7
00:00:14,344 --> 00:00:16,404
The 3D Moon stays in the middle,

8
00:00:16,404 --> 00:00:20,090
and the timeline along the bottom covers the next thirty days.

9
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:21,812
Step one, Site.

10
00:00:21,812 --> 00:00:23,854
Pick a landing site from the list,

11
00:00:23,854 --> 00:00:25,998
search by name, type in coordinates,

12
00:00:25,998 --> 00:00:27,734
or tap one of the best spots

13
00:00:27,734 --> 00:00:29,572
we found for the coming month.

14
00:00:30,222 --> 00:00:31,131
On the Moon,

15
00:00:31,131 --> 00:00:33,807
the gold line points to the Sun from your site,

16
00:00:33,807 --> 00:00:35,827
and the blue line points to Earth.

17
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:37,947
The pill at the top tells you, live,

18
00:00:37,947 --> 00:00:40,270
whether you have power and a radio link.

19
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:42,057
Step two, Date.

20
00:00:42,057 --> 00:00:44,818
The calendar colours every day for your site.

21
00:00:44,818 --> 00:00:48,608
Green means sunlight and Earth together for at least three days.

22
00:00:48,608 --> 00:00:50,015
Amber is power only.

23
00:00:50,015 --> 00:00:51,531
Red means no sunlight.

24
00:00:51,531 --> 00:00:53,101
Tap a day to choose it.

25
00:00:53,751 --> 00:00:54,436
Not sure?

26
00:00:54,436 --> 00:00:57,314
Find the next good date searches the coming year for you.

27
00:00:57,964 --> 00:00:59,153
Step three, Check.

28
00:00:59,153 --> 00:01:01,282
You get a clear verdict at touchdown,

29
00:01:01,282 --> 00:01:04,105
with one light for power and one for Earth contact,

30
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:06,135
and the full assessment underneath.

31
00:01:06,785 --> 00:01:09,310
Press Play, or drag along the timeline,

32
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:11,443
to watch the Sun circle the sky,

33
00:01:11,443 --> 00:01:14,529
and see exactly when power and radio come and go.

34
00:01:15,179 --> 00:01:16,466
Step four, What if.

35
00:01:16,466 --> 00:01:18,370
Move the site by a kilometre or

36
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:19,914
shift the date by a day,

37
00:01:19,914 --> 00:01:22,539
and it tells you in plain words what changes.

38
00:01:23,189 --> 00:01:25,802
For bigger questions, open the Compare Lab.

39
00:01:25,802 --> 00:01:27,189
It ranks your plans,

40
00:01:27,189 --> 00:01:29,909
shows how far each one is from your baseline,

41
00:01:29,909 --> 00:01:32,256
and charts every measure side by side.

42
00:01:32,906 --> 00:01:34,282
Step five, Report.

43
00:01:34,282 --> 00:01:37,376
Your whole scenario on one page, ready to print,

44
00:01:37,376 --> 00:01:39,669
save as a PDF, or share as a link.

45
00:01:40,319 --> 00:01:42,682
And if you're ever stuck, just ask Lumi.

46
00:01:42,682 --> 00:01:44,686
Type a question in plain English,

47
00:01:44,686 --> 00:01:47,615
and Lumi works out the answer with the same engine.

48
00:01:48,265 --> 00:01:49,649
The tutorial, the tour,

49
00:01:49,649 --> 00:01:52,131
and your settings are always in the top right.

50
00:01:52,131 --> 00:01:53,086
Happy landing!
